<title>NETHERLANDS: Commercial Union's DeltaLloyd Q1 97 net up 1.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Commercial Union's DeltaLloyd Q1 97 net up 1.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Q1 to March 31</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	    25.60 vs  25.24</p>
<p>    Net profit			    84.5  vs  83.3</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)		  1.69 vs   1.49</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit from normal ops 117.6  vs 111.5</p>
<p>    Tax				     33.1  vs  28.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Delta Lloyd said it expected full year 1997 profits to be clearly higher than in 1996. Delta Lloyd Verzekeringsgroup NV is a fully-owned subsidiary of Britain's Commercial Union Assurance Co Plc.  </p>
<p>Breakdown of pre-tax profit from normal operations:</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless stated otherwise)</p>
<p>    - Life insurance					88.7 vs 75.5</p>
<p>    - Non-life insurance				  13.2 vs 24.8</p>
<p>    - Holding company activities			12.6 vs  8.1</p>
<p>    - Others						   3.1 vs  3.1</p>
<p>Breakdown of turnover:</p>
<p>    - Premium income life insurance (billions)   795.4 vs 661.0</p>
<p>- Premium income non-life insurance(billions)330.6 vs 315.0</p>
<p>    Other activities					 8.6 vs 8.6</p>
<p>    - Investment income (billions)		   552.9 vs 503.3</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
